1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Why should every Codex workspace have to look the same?

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
I started by trying to change one background.
It grew into a controller for live Wallpaper Engine scenes.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
It is called Codex Wallpaper Skin,
an open-source Windows companion.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Local images, videos, and Wallpaper Engine scenes
can become backgrounds inside Codex itself.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
This is not the desktop showing through.
Codex and the desktop can use different wallpapers independently.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The workflow has three steps: connect Codex,
scan Wallpaper Engine or add local media,

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:00,000
then choose Apply selected.
End users do not need Node.js, Python, or a separate .NET runtime.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Images and ordinary videos load directly.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Complex scenes are rendered by the installed Wallpaper Engine
and delivered to Codex through a local GPU path.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Every wallpaper has different framing, brightness, and color,
so the app provides adaptive colors, focus, and opacity controls,

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:47,000
readability controls, and visual presets that can be saved and assigned.

12
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Live backgrounds can pause or throttle while Codex is hidden.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,000
A watchdog verifies that frames remain visible,
and Doctor provides privacy-redacted diagnostics.

14
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,000
It does not patch official files, chats, or sign-in data,
and the stock background is one click away.

15
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
The public Beta supports Windows 11 x64
and the official x64 OpenAI Codex Store/MSIX desktop package.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Wallpaper Engine is optional unless you use its live scenes
or large video projects.

17
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The project is open source.
If you want a more personal workspace, give it a try.

18
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
If it helps, consider starring the project on GitHub.
